# Line endings: every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every
# OS. Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks files out with
# CRLF, and checks that measure bytes, compare file contents or split on "\n"
# give a different answer on a Windows laptop than in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows command scripts keep CRLF in the working tree.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# Generated: collapsed in GitHub diffs and left out of language stats.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
